{"text": "The closest issuer-concentration check is MSFT: its current weight is 16.0% [f_04daedb8e01a] against a warning level of 15.0% [f_0d4d8b3f4ffd]. That means it is already 1.0% [f_04daedb8e01a] above warning, so there is no room left to warning on the current book.

The breach tier for MSFT is 20.0% [f_021603ece42f]. Relative to the current 16.0% [f_04daedb8e01a], it would take a further 4.0% [f_04daedb8e01a] move up in that name alone, with everything else fixed, to reach breach.

If you cap any single issuer at 8%, the over-cap names are AAPL at 15.2% [f_19eb32c14034], JPM at 14.8% [f_4dc2272f155a], LLY at 12.5% [f_367bb93f14fc], MSFT at 16.0% [f_04daedb8e01a], and GOOGL at 12.4% [f_26e25ae8a924]."}

