{"text": "If we sell half of NVDA and put the proceeds into TLT, gross exposure stays at 100.0% [f_4418e5fab9df]. Technology sector concentration falls to 35.3% [f_e3396b0601ae] from 35.0% [f_3fdfe8cc652b], so that limit gets tighter, not looser.

The book’s beta to QQQ and the stress loss under tech_selloff were not exposed in the scenario output I got. The desk also said one requested item was unavailable: “‘sector_concentration:Technology’ is not a name this desk holds” [f_f09ebd3f92b7], so for the sector limit read I used the limit-check figure instead: 35.3% [f_e3396b0601ae].

What this means for the book: the trade reduces the NVDA concentration check materially — NVDA falls to 2.07% [f_207858caafd1] from 4.18% [f_e8c0de6f8000] — and it modestly increases TLT to 6.14% [f_f802468cd78d]. But the Technology sector remains the binding direction here: it is still elevated, and the scenario data I have does not let me confirm whether the book’s QQQ beta or tech_selloff stress loss improved."}

